{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01KsUq3BnFbE5E4jn9mD3m5w", "type": "tool_result", "content": "{\"contents\":[{\"uri\":\"toolplane://namespace\",\"mimeType\":\"text/markdown\",\"text\":\"# Toolplane execution namespace\\n\\nPython passed to `execute_code` runs against these bindings.\\nEvery binding is async \u2014 always `await` it.\\n\\n## Capability functions\\n- `await orders_get_order(...)` \u2014 mcp:orders/get_order\\n- `await orders_list_order_ids(...)` \u2014 mcp:orders/list_order_ids\\n\\n(Scoped `ns.member` sugar exists only on backends that support it \u2014 this server's default backend binds the flat aliases above instead.)\\n\\nEvery capability, including ones without a binding above, is callable as `await call_tool(\\\"canonical:name\\\", {...params})`. Use `search_capabilities` / `get_capability_schemas` for parameter schemas.\\n\\n## CLI\\nCLI access is disabled in this configuration.\\n\\n## Session\\nVariables persist across execute_code runs on the default backend: assignments and function definitions from one run are simply available in the next \u2014 no save/load step needed.\\n\\n- A failed run keeps the session: prior variables (and statements completed before the error) persist.\\n- A timed-out run is rolled back: the namespace returns to its pre-run state, but capability calls, CLI commands, and saves the run already made stand.\\n- `await reset_session()` clears all session variables after the current run (saved results and artifacts are unaffected).\\n- The session has a memory cap; if a run fails with MemoryError, reassign large variables (`big = None` \u2014 monty has no `del`) or reset.\\n- Assigning a variable named after a Toolplane binding (e.g. `save_result = ...`) is rejected: in a session the assignment would mask the binding until reset.\\n\\n## Result store\\nSession variables already persist between runs; use the store when a value must survive a session reset, cross a backend override, or be read directly as an MCP resource.\\n- `handle = await save_result(value)` \u2014 JSON-shaped values only\\n- `value = await load_result(handle)`\\n- A saved value is also readable directly as the MCP resource `toolplane://results/<handle>` (canonical JSON, no execute_code run needed).\\n\\nHandles persist across execute_code calls within this server session; nothing persists to disk.\\n\\n## Artifact store\\n- `handle = await save_artifact(data, filename=\\\"report.parquet\\\")` \u2014 bytes only (files, images, parquet); JSON-shaped values belong in the result store\\n- `data = await load_artifact(handle)`\\n- A saved artifact is also readable directly as the binary MCP resource `toolplane://artifacts/<handle>`; the execute_code response lists each artifact saved during the run with its URI.\\n\\nArtifacts live on host disk for this server session only and are deleted when the session ends.\"}]}"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8adcc48b-8d48-49f8-8cd8-c57877fddde9", "uuid": "88e67c51-7114-4983-bc8e-9a0bb5ca5685", "timestamp": "2026-07-09T21:08:24.118Z", "tool_use_result": {"contents": [{"uri": "toolplane://namespace", "mimeType": "text/markdown", "text": "# Toolplane execution namespace\n\nPython passed to `execute_code` runs against these bindings.\nEvery binding is async \u2014 always `await` it.\n\n## Capability functions\n- `await orders_get_order(...)` \u2014 mcp:orders/get_order\n- `await orders_list_order_ids(...)` \u2014 mcp:orders/list_order_ids\n\n(Scoped `ns.member` sugar exists only on backends that support it \u2014 this server's default backend binds the flat aliases above instead.)\n\nEvery capability, including ones without a binding above, is callable as `await call_tool(\"canonical:name\", {...params})`. Use `search_capabilities` / `get_capability_schemas` for parameter schemas.\n\n## CLI\nCLI access is disabled in this configuration.\n\n## Session\nVariables persist across execute_code runs on the default backend: assignments and function definitions from one run are simply available in the next \u2014 no save/load step needed.\n\n- A failed run keeps the session: prior variables (and statements completed before the error) persist.\n- A timed-out run is rolled back: the namespace returns to its pre-run state, but capability calls, CLI commands, and saves the run already made stand.\n- `await reset_session()` clears all session variables after the current run (saved results and artifacts are unaffected).\n- The session has a memory cap; if a run fails with MemoryError, reassign large variables (`big = None` \u2014 monty has no `del`) or reset.\n- Assigning a variable named after a Toolplane binding (e.g. `save_result = ...`) is rejected: in a session the assignment would mask the binding until reset.\n\n## Result store\nSession variables already persist between runs; use the store when a value must survive a session reset, cross a backend override, or be read directly as an MCP resource.\n- `handle = await save_result(value)` \u2014 JSON-shaped values only\n- `value = await load_result(handle)`\n- A saved value is also readable directly as the MCP resource `toolplane://results/<handle>` (canonical JSON, no execute_code run needed).\n\nHandles persist across execute_code calls within this server session; nothing persists to disk.\n\n## Artifact store\n- `handle = await save_artifact(data, filename=\"report.parquet\")` \u2014 bytes only (files, images, parquet); JSON-shaped values belong in the result store\n- `data = await load_artifact(handle)`\n- A saved artifact is also readable directly as the binary MCP resource `toolplane://artifacts/<handle>`; the execute_code response lists each artifact saved during the run with its URI.\n\nArtifacts live on host disk for this server session only and are deleted when the session ends."}]}}
